 We count the number of pairs per rank, then multiply by the number of ranks.  There are $\binom{4}{2}$ ways to choose the matching pair per rank, and $4$ ranks, so the number of favorable outcomes is $4\cdot \binom{4}{2}$.  The total number of 3-card hands is $\binom{52}{3}$, so the probability is \[ \frac{4 \cdot \binom{4}{2}}{\binom{52}{3}} = \frac{3}{5525} . \end{align*} >

